title: Slack stops receiving messages after a brief network disconnect; detect and recover automatically
updated_at: "2026-11-02T08:01:54Z"
---
User report: A brief drop in the network connection used by Clawq can disconnect Slack, after which incoming Slack messages no longer reach Clawq.

Reproduction: With the Slack connector running, briefly interrupt network connectivity, restore it, then send a Slack message to Clawq. Check whether inbound delivery resumes without restarting Clawq.

Expected behavior: Detect a lost or stale Slack connection, expose the disconnected/reconnecting state accurately in status and logs, and automatically reconnect with bounded retry/backoff when connectivity returns. Incoming messages sent after recovery must be processed normally without a manual daemon restart or duplicate processing.

Acceptance criteria:
- Exercise a brief network interruption and a stale/half-open connection.
- Verify disconnect detection and automatic reconnect through the production Slack connector path.
- Verify inbound message delivery resumes after network restoration.
- Add regression coverage for disconnect/reconnect and observable connector health.

The precise failure mechanism and treatment of messages sent during the outage require investigation; do not assume Slack replays missed events.

Decision (2026-11-02 batch): Slack lane first, then B832/B833. Verified Socket Mode waits indefinitely on Ws_client.closed, lacks ping/staleness/connect deadlines, and parse_envelope drops Slack disconnect controls without envelope_id. Add production-path disconnect/half-open recovery, bounded backoff, dedup and observable health, using injected transport/clock tests on x-p35.

Independent review caught P1: uncancellable DNS/late transport acquisition can continue after deadline/cancellation, opening resources after memoized cleanup. Fix round1 now adds explicit attempt ownership and deterministic early-cancel/timeout/late-handoff regressions. Earlier recovery28 focused and7765 quick plus minimal compile were green but did not cover this boundary. Review also documented pre-existing remote-Close/callback cleanup limitations in non-Slack Ws_client consumers; Slack finalizer explicitly closes its transport, so those unrelated existing cases remain follow-up notes rather than silently expanding this ticket.

Completed: commits e5faaeb0 and 29ea623e merged as 852c668e after independent scoped PASS. Production Socket Mode handles disconnect/hello controls, bounded connect/ACK/pong waits, half-open detection, 1-30s reconnect, cross-reconnect ACK/dedup, health/status and cancellation cleanup including uncancellable late DNS/TLS/transport results. Focused 35 passed; coordinator exact merged quick gate x-p35 7780 passed in62.620s. Actual Slack outage/service access was not exercised; production-path mocked/loopback evidence covers recovery and post-reconnect delivery. Shared public reference reconciliation stays in pending docs lane.